{
 "item": "HCR-7: the daemon's lifetime (open call 3) and what the daemon and a building server hold",
 "date": "2026-11-27",
 "what_this_file_is": "Measurements taken to put HCR-7's open call (3) to the owner, the same measurements on what was then built, and the footprints README's cost paragraph had left unmeasured since the model moved into the daemon. Real models (the pinned mxfp8 snapshots), scratch copies of the corpora, real MCP servers, the owner's own sessions running beside the runs. Counts, timings and footprints only.",
 "method": "bench/embed_daemon.py lifetime, build-memory and two-models. phys_footprint and phys_footprint_peak from `footprint <pid>`; GB here is MB / 1024. Timings carry 95% percentile-bootstrap intervals and counts 95% Wilson intervals; where a run has two or three values the values are given.",
 "ruling": {
  "asked": "which lifetime rule the shared embed daemon follows, and how long an unused model is kept",
  "the_owner_chose": [
   "(b) Reap + model drop (Recommended)",
   "1,800 s (Recommended)"
  ],
  "put_as": {
   "(a)": "keep the 900 s idle exit; no code change",
   "(b)": "stay while a warm server on high is alive, drop the model after the idle window, exit about 60 s after the last server is gone",
   "(c)": "only a longer idle exit: one constant, exit-only, no heartbeat reading",
   "windows_offered_s": [
    900,
    1800,
    3600
   ]
  }
 },
